   ],
   "source": [
    "ORDER = (0, D, 1)  # read off the ACF/PACF above\n",
    "y = {name: pd.Series(s.to_numpy()) for name, s in prices.items()}  # integer index: trading days have gaps\n",
    "fits, onestep, resid = {}, {}, {}\n",
    "for name in prices:\n",
    "    n = split[name]\n",
    "    res = ARIMA(y[name].iloc[:n], order=ORDER).fit()\n",
    "    pred = res.apply(y[name]).predict()  # frozen training coefficients, one step ahead\n",
    "    fits[name], onestep[name] = res, pred.to_numpy()\n",
    "    resid[name] = (y[name] - pred).to_numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.DataFrame({name: fits[name].params for name in prices}).round(3).rename_axis(f\"ARIMA{ORDER}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1fb4a33f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "θ (`ma.L1`) ≈ −1. The MA term almost cancels the second difference, so the one-step forecast behaves like a random walk with a slowly updated drift."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
